# Line endings.
#
# `text=auto` stores every text file with LF in the repository and checks it out
# with the platform's native endings.
#
# This repository is already stored as LF, because the machine it was created on
# has core.autocrlf=true. That is the point of putting it here: core.autocrlf is
# a per-machine setting, so a contributor with it unset or false on Windows would
# start committing CRLF and every later Linux or CI checkout would report those
# files as wholly rewritten. Committing the intent to the repository makes it
# hold regardless of who clones it.
#
# There is deliberately no `eol=` — the working tree keeps native endings, which
# is what the Excel and editor tooling around this project expects. Only what git
# stores is normalised.
* text=auto

# Scripts that genuinely require CRLF to run on Windows.
*.bat text eol=crlf
*.cmd text eol=crlf

# Binaries — never line-ending converted, never diffed as text.
*.xlsx binary
*.xlsm binary
*.xls  binary
*.zip  binary
*.png  binary
*.jpg  binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif  binary
*.woff  binary
*.woff2 binary
*.ttf   binary

# The source workbooks are inputs to this project, not code it maintains.
# Keep them out of the language breakdown so the repo reads as what it is.
*.xlsm linguist-vendored
*.xlsx linguist-vendored

# The design prototype is marked vendored by a nested .gitattributes inside
# "BOM CAL DESIGN/" — gitattributes patterns cannot express a path containing
# spaces, so a file in the directory is the supported way to do it.

# Generated, and regenerable. Collapsed in diffs and excluded from stats.
demo/boq-report.html linguist-generated
package-lock.json    linguist-generated
